WebGPU on HarmonyOS: Dawn's Vulkan backend, sharing OH_NativeBuffers.

use_dawn and dawn_enable_vulkan left OHOS out, so the GPU process had no
WebGPU decoder and every WebGPU context failed ("Failed to create WebGPU
Context Provider") even with --enable-unsafe-webgpu. Dawn's Vulkan backend
then loads libvulkan.so, as on Android, and is built with the Linux external
memory and semaphore services its C++ calls, since OHOS compiles as Linux in
Dawn.

Textures are shared with the GLES compositor as OH_NativeBuffers, zero-copy.
VK_OHOS_external_memory is Android's AHardwareBuffer import with the names
changed, so on OHOS the AHardwareBuffer SharedTextureMemory descriptor and
feature carry an OH_NativeBuffer, imported with vkGetNativeBufferPropertiesOHOS
and VkImportNativeBufferInfoOHOS (declared in Dawn, as Chromium's Vulkan
headers lack them). Adapters must have that feature. OzoneImageBacking takes
WebGPU's single-plane images (other single-plane images stay GL textures),
DawnOzoneImageRepresentation imports its pixmap's OH_NativeBuffer, and the
two APIs synchronise with sync fds: VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd on Dawn's
side, EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync on ANGLE's. libsync is not built here,
so the one sync_merge() needed is the SYNC_IOC_MERGE ioctl.

Experimental and behind --enable-unsafe-webgpu.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 (Dawn 8597a1aaec54).

